\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\ src/pow.fam — memory-hard proof-of-work hash (Poseidon2-BabyBear seed + walk).
\ Verifier side: given a block header and the pre-expanded bible table, recompute
\ the PoW hash. Design (see design discussion): ONE strong Poseidon2 at the start
\ conditions the input; the 128-round walk is a cheap, in-circuit-friendly BabyBear
\ FIELD-ADD mixing over a high-entropy table, with a running accumulator threading
\ every read into ONE depth-32 dependent chain. NO Poseidon2 in the loop (that was
\ compute-hard, not memory-hard, and a huge AIR); NO finalization hash (PoW needs
\ no-cheap-path, not a uniform output — the data-dependent indexing supplies that,
\ and additive mixing keeps the output uniform regardless of table bias). All ops
\ are BabyBear field ops, so it runs on the rv32i verifier and the AIR stays cheap.
\ Built on p2hash (poseidon2.fam) + fadd (babybear.fam); compile AFTER both.
\   powhash ( hdr n table mask out scr -- )
\     out(8w) = w;  w = p2hash(hdr,n);  acc = 0 (kept in scr[0]);
\     128x: j = (r&7);  idx = (w[j]+acc)&mask;  w[j] += table[idx];  acc += w[j].
\     scr >= 0xA0 (p2hash scratch; scr[0] reused for acc after the seed).
\ ROUNDS = 128 (0x80): the walk dwarfs the one-time seed hash so an ASIC stays
\ memory-bound; even a fast-banked-SRAM build is pushed toward its ~67% floor.
\ table = NSLOT single-word field entries (NOT 8-word slots); built off-circuit from
\ the bible seed by src/tblexpand.fam (chained blake2s), cached on disk.
\ Production mask = 0x3FFFFF (4Mi slots = 16 MiB). Difficulty/target
\ compare folds all 8 words (field add) downstream. Python ref: tmp/pos2/powref.py.
\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

: powhash ( hdr n table mask out scr -- )
  5 lit pick 5 lit pick 3 lit pick 3 lit pick p2hash   \ out = p2hash(hdr,n)
  0 lit over !                                          \ acc := 0  (in scr[0])
  80 lit 0 lit do
    i 7 lit and 2 lit lshift                            \ j4 = (r&7)<<2
    2 lit pick +                                        \ wp = out + j4
    dup @                                               \ wv = w[j]
    2 lit pick @                                        \ acc = scr[0]
    over fadd                                           \ s  = wv + acc
    5 lit pick and                                      \ idx = s & mask
    2 lit lshift  6 lit pick + @                        \ tv = table[idx]
    over fadd                                           \ nw = wv + tv
    3 lit pick @ over fadd                              \ acc' = acc + nw
    4 lit pick !                                        \ scr[0] := acc'
    nip swap !                                          \ w[j] := nw
  loop
  2drop 2drop 2drop ;

\ powlt ( out target -- flag )  -1 iff out < target as a 256-bit number (8 words, out[0]
\ MOST significant), else 0.  The PoW difficulty test: a hash is valid iff out < target.
\ 256-bit (~248-bit, words < p) target gives the full difficulty range realistic mining
\ needs; a single field-element fold would cap difficulty at ~2^31 (way too coarse).
: powlt ( out target -- flag )
  0 lit                                        \ res = 0
  8 lit 0 lit do
    2 lit pick 7 lit i - 4 lit * + @           \ a = out[7-i]
    2 lit pick 7 lit i - 4 lit * + @           \ b = target[7-i]
    2dup u< if 2drop drop FFFFFFFF lit
    else 2dup swap u< if 2drop drop 0 lit
    else 2drop then then
  loop
  nip nip ;

\ mine ( hdr n table mask target out scr start -- nonce found )  sweep the LAST header
\ word (nonce = hdr[n-1]) from `start` up to 0xFFFFFFFF until powhash(...) < target
\ (target = ptr to an 8-word 256-bit threshold). Returns ( winning-nonce -1 ) on a hit
\ (hdr[n-1] + out hold it) or ( 0xFFFFFFFF 0 ) when the 32-bit nonce space is exhausted
\ with no hit — the caller then bumps the header's aux-hash field and re-mines (the
\ extra entropy, Bitcoin-style). `start` enables resume / chunked sweeps. scr>=0xC8.
\ This fam/QEMU impl is the canonical/reference miner (whole reference impl is fam — no
\ Rust); a faster miner reimplements the same powhash+mine in hardware (external). Block
\ production also needs the STARK proof (separate fam work). ctx (9w) carved from scr at
\ scr+0xA0 (above powhash's 0xA0 region -> NO heap alloc / no per-call leak):
\   +0 hdr +4 n +8 table +C mask +10 target +14 out +18 scr +1C nonce +20 found.
: mine ( hdr n table mask target out scr start -- nonce found )
  over A0 lit +                \ ctx = scr + 0xA0  (scr at depth1; reuse caller scratch, no leak)
  1 lit pick over 1C lit + !   \ nonce = start
  2 lit pick over 18 lit + !   3 lit pick over 14 lit + !   4 lit pick over 10 lit + !
  5 lit pick over C lit + !    6 lit pick over 8 lit + !    7 lit pick over 4 lit + !
  8 lit pick over !
  nip nip nip nip nip nip nip nip
  begin
    dup @  over 4 lit + @ 1 lit - 2 lit lshift +  over 1C lit + @  swap !   \ hdr[n-1] = nonce
    dup @  over 4 lit + @  2 lit pick 8 lit + @  3 lit pick C lit + @  4 lit pick 14 lit + @  5 lit pick 18 lit + @  powhash
    dup 14 lit + @  over 10 lit + @  powlt  over 20 lit + !                 \ found = (out < target); store
    dup 20 lit + @ 0 lit =  over 1C lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit u<  and            \ keepgoing = !found AND nonce<MAX
  while
    dup 1C lit + dup @ 1 lit + swap !                                       \ nonce++
  repeat
  dup 20 lit + @  swap 1C lit + @  swap ;                                   \ ( nonce found ) ; found 0 = exhausted

Test {
pow0 {
  80 lit alloc
  661A8509 lit over !
  5AF5F320 lit over 4 lit + !
  0FB1F71D lit over 8 lit + !
  620BE6E4 lit over C lit + !
  15E8C410 lit over 10 lit + !
  1B25FA77 lit over 14 lit + !
  704FC667 lit over 18 lit + !
  1435DC86 lit over 1C lit + !
  2630D9B9 lit over 20 lit + !
  612BD03A lit over 24 lit + !
  76F7A1C7 lit over 28 lit + !
  22C93B55 lit over 2C lit + !
  60704580 lit over 30 lit + !
  4C2549D7 lit over 34 lit + !
  69077C76 lit over 38 lit + !
  2717D33D lit over 3C lit + !
  017D58A0 lit over 40 lit + !
  371A144D lit over 44 lit + !
  4F2C4ED1 lit over 48 lit + !
  21BA9FD1 lit over 4C lit + !
  75FF7BA0 lit over 50 lit + !
  3834848C lit over 54 lit + !
  1AD5D410 lit over 58 lit + !
  7609B55E lit over 5C lit + !
  672844C6 lit over 60 lit + !
  586FEF7F lit over 64 lit + !
  2B97AE5A lit over 68 lit + !
  18EEA67B lit over 6C lit + !
  29251983 lit over 70 lit + !
  747E3E37 lit over 74 lit + !
  1A516249 lit over 78 lit + !
  16004349 lit over 7C lit + !
  14 lit alloc
  11111111 lit over !
  22222222 lit over 4 lit + !
  33333333 lit over 8 lit + !
  44444444 lit over C lit + !
  55555555 lit over 10 lit + !
  20 lit alloc
  C8 lit alloc                 \ scr: 0xA0 for powhash + 0x24 for mine's 9-word ctx
  20 lit alloc
  53BB87FC lit over !
  4DAE675E lit over 4 lit + !
  55B67BCC lit over 8 lit + !
  55AB4075 lit over C lit + !
  747B3CF4 lit over 10 lit + !
  3AF55CFA lit over 14 lit + !
  4CBAB861 lit over 18 lit + !
  660F83FA lit over 1C lit + !
  \ stack: table header out scr eOUT
  3 lit pick  5 lit  6 lit pick  0000001F lit  6 lit pick  6 lit pick  powhash
  2 lit pick 1 lit pick cmp8  1 lit asrt_eq
  \ build the 256-bit target [0x0F000000, FFFFFFFF x7]  ( -> stack: table header out scr eOUT target )
  20 lit alloc
  0F000000 lit over !          FFFFFFFF lit over 4 lit + !
  FFFFFFFF lit over 8 lit + !  FFFFFFFF lit over C lit + !
  FFFFFFFF lit over 10 lit + ! FFFFFFFF lit over 14 lit + !
  FFFFFFFF lit over 18 lit + ! FFFFFFFF lit over 1C lit + !
  \ FOUND: mine(header,5,table,0x1F,target,out,scr,start=0) -> ( nonce=5  found=-1 )
  4 lit pick 5 lit 7 lit pick 0000001F lit 4 lit pick 8 lit pick 8 lit pick 0 lit mine
  FFFFFFFF lit asrt_eq  5 lit asrt_eq
  \ EXHAUST: refill target = 0 (impossible) ; start near MAX -> ( nonce=FFFFFFFF  found=0 )
  0 lit over !          0 lit over 4 lit + !
  0 lit over 8 lit + !  0 lit over C lit + !
  0 lit over 10 lit + ! 0 lit over 14 lit + !
  0 lit over 18 lit + ! 0 lit over 1C lit + !
  4 lit pick 5 lit 7 lit pick 0000001F lit 4 lit pick 8 lit pick 8 lit pick FFFFFFFD lit mine
  0 lit asrt_eq  FFFFFFFF lit asrt_eq
  drop
  2drop 2drop drop
}
}
